OL,3,GNEWSAI was told epilepsy drug wouldn't
OL,4,Aharm my baby. Now we live with the
OL,5,Aconsequences
OL,6,
OL,7,FRosemary Nayler says she was repeatedly
OL,8,Ftold that taking the epilepsy drug
OL,9,Fsodium valproate while pregnant would
OL,10,Fnot affect her unborn child.
OL,12,FBut it is thought thousands of children
OL,13,Fin the UK have been left with
OL,14,Fdisabilities caused by the medication
OL,15,Fsince the 1970s.
OL,17,FHer daughter, Nadia Williams, is now
OL,18,F37, registered blind and deaf, is
OL,19,Fautistic and has mobility issues.
